C:\Users\Jason\Documents\Jason\Orchestrator_Harness\Firmware\fresh-experiments\S11_20260821-plan2-suite-012\.agent-workspace\suite012_s11_boreal_replacement_002_codex.jsonl:109:{"type":"assistant","uuid":"6b650666-26f5-4448-900f-693638c60b25","session_id":"cb916473-1240-43a0-9a58-d24373d5f240","parent_tool_use_id":null,"message":{"id":"6b650666-26f5-4448-900f-693638c60b25","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-v4-flash:0731-cloud","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The server routed both NRF-A and NRF-B to fresh setup (profiles: [] — isolated root confirmed, no package `.firm` leakage). The routes give me:\n- NRF-A: board_id `nrf_a`, connection `probe:683710208`, serial `000683710208` (COM16)\n- NRF-B: board_id `nrf_b`, connection `probe:683854191`, serial `000683854191` (COM15)\n\nRequired user facts (all supplied by the sealed spec):\n- exact package-level MCU part number: `nRF52840-QIAA` (spec: truthfully established)\n- authoritative local datasheet PDF: `Nano_BLE_MCU-nRF52840_PS_v1.1.pdf` (hash verified c619e336...)\n- UART: yes, 115200 (spec: UART requirement; VCOM COM16/COM15)\n- authorization: recorded delegation `AUTHORIZED_FOR_20260821_PLAN2_SUITE_012_MANAGER_014` covers ordinary non-destructive setup\n- probe choice: NRF-A → 683710208, NRF-B → 683854191\n- UART choice: NRF-A → 000683710208 (COM16), NRF-B → 000683854191 (COM15)\n\nNow load the setup tool for nrf_a, then call the all-NULL board_setup-plan, then populate. Let me load the setup tool first.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0}}}
